---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Projects — Guy Friley / 0xguy';
const description = 'All my public projects — what I am currently building, what I am learning on, and what is archived.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
    <h1>What I'm building</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      A directory of public repos. Detailed writeups for most of these live on the <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Home" class="ext-link">notebook</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Currently building</h2>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>sf-tui</h3>
      <p class="meta">go · bubble tea · salesforce · terminal ui</p>
      <p>
        A keyboard-driven terminal UI for Salesforce developers: SOQL with live autocomplete, anonymous Apex, debug-log tailing, an Apex test runner with coverage, a permission explorer, an API-limits dashboard, and field-level schema compare between orgs. Runs on top of the <code>sf</code> CLI and reuses your existing auths. Installable via Homebrew or Scoop.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/sf-tui" class="ext-link">github →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Homelab</h3>
      <p class="meta">proxmox · tailscale · self-hosting · security</p>
      <p>
        Full build-out from a dormant PC and spare hardware: virtualization layer, network segmentation, observability, security hardening.
        Diagrams, configs, and postmortems live in the <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Homelab" class="ext-link">Homelab section of the notebook</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>dm_toolkit &amp; dm_toolkit_extension</h3>
      <p class="meta">d&amp;d · full-stack · browser extension</p>
      <p>
        A Dungeon Master toolkit with a companion browser extension. Hobby-driven, but an excellent excuse to practice shipping end-to-end — extension APIs, packaging, state management.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/dm_toolkit" class="ext-link">dm_toolkit</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/dm_toolkit_extension" class="ext-link">extension</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>sf-claude-studio</h3>
      <p class="meta">claude code · salesforce · agents</p>
      <p>
        Turns a single Claude Code session into a Salesforce delivery studio: 10 agents, 15 skills, 7 hooks, and path-scoped rule sets covering Apex, LWC, flow, integration, data, QA, security and DevOps.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/sf-claude-studio" class="ext-link">github →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Pittsburgh history maps</h3>
      <p class="meta">leaflet · github pages · local history</p>
      <p>
        Interactive maps of Swisshelm Park and Frick Park with historical photos, events, lost features, and old map overlays.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/swisshelm-park-history" class="ext-link">Swisshelm Park</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/frick-park-history" class="ext-link">Frick Park</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Death by ZIP Code</h3>
      <p class="meta">data viz · data essay · pittsburgh</p>
      <p>
        An interactive data essay on Pittsburgh's overdose crisis.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/death-by-zip-code" class="ext-link">github →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>This site (0xguy07.github.io)</h3>
      <p class="meta">astro · github pages · tokyo night</p>
      <p>
        Hand-rolled Astro site with a Tokyo Night + Tech Orange theme that matches the <code>publish.css</code> on the Obsidian notebook. Deployed via GitHub Actions.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/0xguy07.github.io" class="ext-link">github →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Writeups</h2>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>System Hardening</h3>
      <p class="meta">linux · ssh · ufw · fail2ban</p>
      <p>
        Locking down any Debian-based system — SSH daemon config, UFW firewall rules, Fail2Ban, automatic updates, service auditing. The playbook I run on every new lab host.
        <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Homelab/System+Hardening" class="ext-link">Read →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>SSH Key-Based Authentication</h3>
      <p class="meta">linux · ssh · cryptography</p>
      <p>
        How Ed25519 key pairs replace password login, the full generate → copy → verify workflow, and why Ed25519 beats RSA everywhere except legacy compatibility.
        <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Linux/SSH+Key-Based+Authentication" class="ext-link">Read →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Raspberry Pi 5 hardening</h3>
      <p class="meta">linux · raspberry pi · security</p>
      <p>
        Step-by-step walk-through of hardening a fresh Pi 5: user hygiene, SSH key auth, Fail2Ban, firewall rules. The applied version of <em>System Hardening</em>.
        <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Homelab/Hardening+a+Raspberry+Pi" class="ext-link">Read →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Flipper Zero × Security+ Learning Path</h3>
      <p class="meta">security+ · hardware · hands-on</p>
      <p>
        A 7-phase, 14-week curriculum mapping Flipper Zero labs (IR, RFID/NFC, Sub-GHz, WiFi with the ESP32 Marauder, BadUSB) to CompTIA Security+ SY0-701 exam domains. Turns a pocket device into a study aid.
        <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Cybersecurity/Flipper+Zero+and+Security%2B+Learning+Path" class="ext-link">Read →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Learning projects</h2>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Zero to Mastery Python 2026</h3>
      <p class="meta">python · coursework</p>
      <p>
        Coursework repository for the Zero to Mastery Python curriculum — the scaffolding for everything else I build in Python.
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/Zero_to_Mastery_Python_2026" class="ext-link">github →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>guessing-game</h3>
      <p class="meta">python · learning-in-public</p>
      <p>
        My "escape from tutorial hell" project — small, finished, iterated on. Taught me how to catch <code>ValueError</code> properly and why input-range validation matters.
        <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/0xguy/Programming/Programming+-+Create+a+Guessing+Game+with+Python" class="ext-link">writeup</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/guessing-game" class="ext-link">github</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Archive</h2>
    <p>
      Older learning repos from 2019–2021. Kept public for history — Terraform exploration, Python bootcamp exercises, PowerShell codewars, intro CS work.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/learn-terraform" class="ext-link">learn-terraform</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/learning-terraform-up-and-running" class="ext-link">learning-terraform-up-and-running</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/learning-terraform-mtc" class="ext-link">learning-terraform-mtc</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/learning-python" class="ext-link">learning-python</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/learning-crash-course-on-python" class="ext-link">learning-crash-course-on-python</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/codewars-powershell" class="ext-link">codewars-powershell</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/list_append" class="ext-link">list_append</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/0xguy07/parisi_cafe" class="ext-link">parisi_cafe</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>
      Full repo list: <a href="https://github.com/0xguy07?tab=repositories" class="ext-link">github.com/0xguy07</a>.
    </p>
  </footer>

</Base>
